      </div>
      <div>
        <a name="definitions" id="definitions"></a>
        <h1>3.<span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>Definitions</h1>
        <div><a name="terms_defined_elsewhere" id="terms_defined_elsewhere"></a><h2>3.1.<span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>Terms defined elsewhere</h2>
<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_2cb75602-135c-f103-a832-9261baf496e1" id="_2cb75602-135c-f103-a832-9261baf496e1"></a>This Recommendation uses the following terms defined elsewhere:</p>
<div><a name="term_cloud_computing" id="term_cloud_computing"></a><p class="TermNum"><a name="term_cloud_computing" id="term_cloud_computing"></a><b>3.1.1.<span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span><b>cloud computing</b>:</b>Paradigm for enabling network access to a scalable and elastic pool of shareable physical or virtual resources with self-service provisioning and administration on-demand.</p>



 </div>

<div><a name="term_cloud_service" id="term_cloud_service"></a><p class="TermNum"><a name="term_cloud_service" id="term_cloud_service"></a><b>3.1.2.<span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span><b>cloud service</b>:</b>One or more capabilities offered via cloud computing invoked using a defined interface.</p>



 </div>

<div><a name="term_cloud_service_customer" id="term_cloud_service_customer"></a><p class="TermNum"><a name="term_cloud_service_customer" id="term_cloud_service_customer"></a><b>3.1.3.<span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span><b>cloud service customer</b>:</b>Party which is in a business relationship for thepurpose of using cloud services.</p>



 </div>

<div><a name="term_cloud_service_provider" id="term_cloud_service_provider"></a><p class="TermNum"><a name="term_cloud_service_provider" id="term_cloud_service_provider"></a><b>3.1.4.<span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span><b>cloud service provider</b>:</b>Party which makes cloud services available.</p>



 </div>

<div><a name="term_physical_resource" id="term_physical_resource"></a><p class="TermNum"><a name="term_physical_resource" id="term_physical_resource"></a><b>3.1.5.<span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span><b>physical resource</b>:</b>A physical asset for computation, storage and/or networking.</p>





 <div class="Note"><a name="_a29e9906-0ff1-f853-beb8-88f231cb5212" id="_a29e9906-0ff1-f853-beb8-88f231cb5212"></a><p class="Note"><span class="termnote_label">NOTE &#x2013; </span>Components, systems and equipment can be regarded as physical resources</p></div></div>
</div>
        <div><a name="terms_defined_in_this_recommendation" id="terms_defined_in_this_recommendation"></a><h2>3.2.<span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>Terms defined in this recommendation</h2>
<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_e5a3a498-5d65-3b79-729e-f4f7bff7eac2" id="_e5a3a498-5d65-3b79-729e-f4f7bff7eac2"></a>This Recommendation defines the following terms:</p>
<div><a name="term_physical_machine" id="term_physical_machine"></a><p class="TermNum"><a name="term_physical_machine" id="term_physical_machine"></a><b>3.2.1.<span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span><b>physical machine</b>:</b>A type of computing machine providing physical resources.</p>



 <div class="Note"><a name="_d1e5c351-d84f-f139-3c5a-ade1e35313c5" id="_d1e5c351-d84f-f139-3c5a-ade1e35313c5"></a><p class="Note"><span class="termnote_label">NOTE &#x2013; </span>A computing machine provides allocation and scheduling of processing resources. Types of computing machine are physical or virtual <a href="#ITU-T_Y.3510">[ITU-T&#xA0;Y.3510]</a>.</p></div></div>
</div>
      </div>
      <div class="Symbols">
